1. Check if there's any data at all, no filter
az batch pool supported-images list --query "length(@)"
If this prints 0 or errors, the problem is upstream of my --query filter — likely the Batch data-plane session isn't authenticated in this terminal:

az batch account login --name "$BATCH" --resource-group "$RG"
az batch pool supported-images list --query "length(@)"
Retry the count after logging in — if it's still 0, something's off with account access; if it jumps to a real number (there should be dozens), the filter step below will now work too.

